title: The deliberate event the detection is tested against
subtitle: week-12-detections-as-code — captured 2026-11-07, identifiers masked
width: 1000
---
# az role assignment create fails with MissingSubscription on CLI 2.86.0
# here -- for `list` as well as `create` -- while the same call through the
# ARM API works. So the trigger goes through az rest.

$ date -u +"TRIGGER at %Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ"
TRIGGER at 2026-11-07T15:17:43Z

$ az rest --method put \
    --url ".../roleAssignments/$RA?api-version=2022-04-01" \
    --body @ra.json \
    --query "{role:properties.roleDefinitionId,
              type:properties.principalType,
              created:properties.createdOn}"

{
  "created": "2026-11-07T15:17:45.5404434Z",
  "role": "/subscriptions/<guid>/providers/Microsoft.Authorization/roleDefinitions/<guid>",
  "type": "User"
}

# Reader, at the week's own resource group scope. Revoked by cleanup.sh
# BEFORE the destroy, explicitly rather than implicitly -- a lab that
# demonstrates privilege escalation and leaves the privilege behind has
# not finished.
#
# This is the INPUT to the test. It is not evidence that anything detected
# it; that is figure 06.
